  "notes": "CardDemo's nightly (#8885, Graveyard Shift 2): POSTTRAN, INTCALC, TRANBKP, COMBTRAN, CREASTMT, TRANIDX as one chain from CardDemo's shipped data. What the chain claims: each step is proven as its own case (COBOL under GnuCOBOL, then the port; an IDCAMS step on the det model with the Java runtime compared line for line), and what a step reads is the COBOL side's output of the step before, the same bytes the Java side is given; every compared output and condition code must be equal on both sides. The oracle is GnuCOBOL plus the models, not z/OS. The wiring (which step feeds which, the GDG generations BKUP / SYSTRAN / COMBINED, the empty KSDS TRANBKP redefines and COMBTRAN STEP10 reloads) is written here from the case, not read from the JCL (Graveyard Shift 3). CREASTMT: STEP010's OUTREC is 328 bytes under a 350-byte DD LRECL, so IBM ends the step (ICE043A, register F4, no pad guessed) and COND=(0,NE) bypasses STEP020 and CBSTM03A; TRANIDX is its own JCL job and still runs. The TRANBKP deck is the JCL's, including its DELETE of the AIX (an absent entry: code 8, then SET MAXCC = 0; #8885 slice 2); TRANIDX is refused by name by the model (BLDINDEX over this chain's TRANSACT, whose busiest alternate key needs a 5055-byte record over RECORDSIZE 350, IBM's outcome not stated), so the nightly is not proven over its last step."
